  ($hc$how-to-add-tips-advances-and-extra-pay$hc$, $hc$How to add tips, advances and extra pay$hc$, $hc$admin$hc$, array['entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Share tips, record a salary advance and add one-off earnings or deductions to payroll.$hc$, $hc$Tips, advances and one-off items change the amount a person is paid. Add them before you approve the month.

## Steps
To share tips:
1. Open **Payroll** and tap **Distribute tips**.
2. Choose the **Branch** and the **From** and **To** dates.
3. Choose how tips are split: **Equal shares** or **By role points**.
4. Choose how tips reach staff.
5. Check the preview and tap **Confirm distribution**.
   ![Distribute tips panel](shot:payroll-tips-drawer "1. Branch and period | 2. Split method | 3. Preview | 4. Confirm distribution")

To record a salary advance:
1. Tap **Advances**.
2. Under **New advance**, choose the **Employee**, **Amount**, **Paid out on** and **Repayments start**.
3. Set the **Number of instalments** and a **Reason**.
4. Tap **Save advance**.
   ![Salary advances panel](shot:payroll-advances-drawer "1. Employee | 2. Amount | 3. Instalments | 4. Save advance")

To add a one-off earning or deduction:
1. Select people in the table.
2. Tap **Adjust**. The panel is called **Add earning or deduction**.
3. Choose **Type**, **What for** and **Amount**.
4. Choose **This amount for each employee** or **Split this total across them**.
5. Type the **Reason (shown on the payslip)**.
6. Tap **Preview**, then tap **Add to** and the number of employees.

## What happens next
Advance repayments are taken from payroll automatically. The advance form reminds you that written consent is needed and no interest may be charged.

One-off items appear in the person's record under **One-off earnings and deductions**, and on the payslip. Earnings include Bonus, Commission, Reimbursement, **Correction (underpaid)**, End-of-service gratuity, Leave encashment, Notice pay and Other earning. Deductions include Cash shortage, Uniform, Damage, Approved fine and Other deduction. Damage and fines have legal limits shown in the list.

Role points for tips are set in **Settings**.

## Common problems
- **Some positions have no role points.** One point is used. Set points in **Settings**.
- **Preview shows 0.** Nobody selected can take the item. Check the status of each person.
- **I added a wrong item.** Open the person and tap **Remove** next to it, if they are still in Draft.

## Related guides
- [How to run payroll for a month](/help/how-to-run-payroll)
- [How to correct payroll after approval](/help/how-to-correct-payroll-after-approval)
- [How to enter hours and tips for payroll](/help/how-to-enter-hours-and-tips-for-payroll)$hc$, array['how-to-run-payroll','how-to-correct-payroll-after-approval','how-to-enter-hours-and-tips-for-payroll']::text[], $hc$/payroll$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-approve-or-decline-leave$hc$, $hc$How to approve or decline leave$hc$, $hc$manager$hc$, array['location_manager','entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Decide leave requests, deal with a low balance and cover shifts on leave days.$hc$, $hc$Leave requests wait for you on the **Leave** page. A Branch Manager decides for their branch. Company Admins and Owners can decide for the whole company.

## Steps
1. Tap **Leave** in the menu.
2. Look at **Awaiting your decision**.
   ![Leave awaiting your decision](shot:leave-awaiting-decision "1. Request details | 2. Reject | 3. Approve | 4. Recent decisions")
3. Read the name, dates and days asked.
4. Tap **Approve** or **Reject**.
5. For **Reject**, confirm "Reject ...’s leave?".
6. If the person has too few days, you see "Not enough leave balance." Admins can tap **Override & approve…**, type the **Override reason (required)** and tap **Confirm override**.
7. Check **Recent decisions** at the bottom.

## What happens next
Approving says "Leave approved — balance updated." Rejecting says "Leave rejected." The employee gets a notification.

If the person still has shifts on those days, a yellow box says they were not cancelled. Tap **Find cover** for each one. Shifts not shared yet will not be shared with staff on leave days.

Status words are **Pending**, **Approved**, **Rejected** and **Cancelled**.

## Common problems
- **Approve fails with "Insufficient balance".** Reject the request, or ask a Company Admin or Owner to override.
- **I do not see any requests.** Branch Managers only see their own branch.
- **The person says it is still pending.** Check it is not in another branch's queue.

## Related guides
- [How to request leave](/help/how-to-request-leave)
- [How to find cover and handle swap requests](/help/how-to-find-cover-and-handle-swap-requests)
- [How to manage leave balances](/help/how-to-manage-leave-balances)$hc$, array['how-to-request-leave','how-to-find-cover-and-handle-swap-requests','how-to-manage-leave-balances']::text[], $hc$/leave$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-ask-an-employee-for-missing-details$hc$, $hc$How to ask an employee for missing details$hc$, $hc$manager$hc$, array['location_manager','entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Tick what is missing and send the request to one employee or to everyone.$hc$, $hc$When a person is missing documents, bank details or personal details, you can ask them in one go. The app only asks for the items you tick. The request appears on the employee's Home screen.

## Steps
To ask one employee:
1. Open **People** and tap the person's name.
2. Find the card **Requests to** their name.
3. Tap **Ask for missing details**.
   ![Requests card on an employee record](shot:ask-requests-card "1. Ask for missing details | 2. Ask for something")
4. Tick what to ask for under **Documents**, **Bank details** and **Personal details**. Tap **Select all** to tick everything.
5. Add a **Note for them (optional)**.
6. Add a **Due date (optional)**.
7. Tap **Ask for** and the number of items.
   ![Ask for missing details tick-list](shot:ask-missing-ticklist "1. Groups | 2. Select all | 3. Note | 4. Due date | 5. Ask for button")

To ask for one thing only:
1. On the same card, tap **Ask for something**.
2. Choose **Upload a document**, **Bank / payment details** or **Missing information**.
3. Choose the document or tick the details.
4. Tap **Send request**.

To ask everyone:
1. Open **People**.
2. Set **Filter by branch** if you want only one branch.
3. Tap **Ask for missing details** at the top.
4. Tick the items, then tap the **Ask for** button.
   ![Ask everyone tick-list](shot:ask-many-ticklist "2. Ticks | 3. Ask for button")

## What happens next
The app says who was asked. The employee sees **Your manager needs something** on Home with a button such as **Upload document**, **Add bank details** or **Fill in details**.

On the employee record, open requests show **Waiting**, or **Overdue** after the due date. Tap **Cancel** to withdraw one. Tap **Show finished requests** to see **Done** and **Cancelled** requests.

Each person is only asked for what they are actually missing. Items already asked show "Already asked" and cannot be ticked again. If nothing is missing, the app says the person "isn’t missing anything".

Branch Managers cannot ask for sensitive documents. These show "Owner or Company Admin only". When a Branch Manager asks for everyone, only their own branch is included.

## Common problems
- **The tick box is greyed out.** It says "Already asked", or only an Owner or Company Admin can ask for it.
- **"Nothing new to send".** Nobody is missing the ticked items, or they have already been asked.
- **The employee says they cannot see it.** Ask them to open **Home**. The request is there.
- **I cannot choose a passport.** Passport, visa, Emirates ID and contracts can only be asked for by a Company Admin or Owner.

## Related guides
- [How to view and manage your team](/help/how-to-view-and-manage-your-team)
- [Update your profile and contact details](/help/update-your-profile-and-contact-details)
- [How to upload or renew a document](/help/how-to-upload-or-renew-a-document)$hc$, array['how-to-view-and-manage-your-team','update-your-profile-and-contact-details','how-to-upload-or-renew-a-document']::text[], $hc$/employees$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-ask-for-cover-or-take-a-colleagues-shift$hc$, $hc$How to ask for cover or take a colleague's shift$hc$, $hc$employee$hc$, array['staff','shift_supervisor']::text[], $hc$Ask a colleague to cover your shift, take someone else's shift, or answer a manager's offer.$hc$, $hc$If you cannot work a shift, you can ask a colleague to cover it. You can also pick up shifts that others need covered. A manager must approve every swap.

## Steps
To ask for cover:
1. Open **Schedule**.
2. Find the shift in **Upcoming shifts**.
3. Tap **Ask for cover**.
4. Type a **Note for whoever picks this up (optional)**.
5. Tap **Send request**.
   ![Ask for cover note box](shot:cover-ask "1. Ask for cover | 2. Note field | 3. Send request")

To take a colleague's shift:
1. Scroll to **Colleagues need cover**.
2. Find a shift you can work.
3. Tap **I’ll cover it**.
   ![Colleagues need cover list](shot:cover-colleagues "1. Shift row | 2. I’ll cover it")

To pick up an unfilled shift:
1. Scroll to **Open shifts**.
2. Tap **Take this shift**.

To answer a manager's offer:
1. At the top, look for **Can you cover?**
2. Tap **Accept shift** to take it, or **Decline**.
   ![Can you cover offers](shot:cover-offers "1. Offer details | 2. Decline | 3. Accept shift")

To cancel your cover request:
1. Scroll to **Your cover requests**.
2. Tap **Cancel** next to the request.

## What happens next
Your request shows one of these words:
- **Waiting for a colleague**: nobody has taken it yet.
- **Waiting for manager**: a colleague said they will cover it. A manager must now approve.
- **Approved**: the shift is moved to your colleague.
- **Not approved**: the shift stays yours.
- **Cancelled**: you cancelled it.

You can cancel while it is "Waiting for a colleague" or "Waiting for manager". If you cancel, the shift stays yours.

When you accept a manager's offer, the app says "Thanks — the shift is yours." and the shift moves to your upcoming shifts. If you decline, your manager is told.

## Common problems
- **I do not see Ask for cover.** Your company may have shift handovers switched off. You will not see **Colleagues need cover** either. Ask your manager.
- **The app will not let me take a shift.** The app tells you the reason, for example you already work then or are on leave.
- **"This offer is closed."** Someone else took it or the manager withdrew it.
- **I am sick today.** Use **Can’t come in** instead. See the schedule guide.

## Related guides
- [How to view your schedule and shifts](/help/how-to-view-your-schedule-and-shifts)
- [How to request leave](/help/how-to-request-leave)$hc$, array['how-to-view-your-schedule-and-shifts','how-to-request-leave']::text[], $hc$/schedules$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-build-and-share-a-weekly-schedule$hc$, $hc$How to build and share a weekly schedule$hc$, $hc$manager$hc$, array['location_manager','entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Add shifts on the week board, check them and share the week with staff.$hc$, $hc$The **Schedules** page shows a week board. You add shifts, check them, then share them with staff. Staff cannot see a shift until you share it.

## Steps
1. Tap **Schedules** in the menu.
2. Choose your branch in **Branch**.
3. Use the arrows and **This week** to pick the week.
   ![Schedules week board](shot:schedules-week-board "1. Branch | 2. Week arrows / This week | 3. New shift | 4. Not shared shift | 5. Share week with staff")
4. Tap **New shift**.
5. Choose the **Branch**, **Date**, **Start** and **End**.
6. Set **Break (min)** and **Role (optional)** if needed.
7. In **Assign to (optional — leave blank to post as open)**, choose a person. Leave it blank for an open shift.
   ![New shift form](shot:schedules-new-shift "1. Branch/Date | 2. Start/End | 3. Assign to | 4. Create shift")
8. Tap **Create shift**.
9. Check the week board. Shifts that are not shared show **Not shared**.
10. Tap **Share week with staff** and confirm. You must choose one branch first.
    ![Share week with staff button](shot:schedules-share-week "1. Share week with staff (n) | 2. Confirm")

## What happens next
New shifts are drafts. On the board they show **Not shared**. The top of the page says how many are "not shared yet".

After you share, staff see them. The board then shows **Shared**. A shift you changed after sharing shows **Changed**. A cancelled shift shows **Cancelled**.

The app says "Shared ... shift(s) with staff." If someone is on approved leave on that day, their shift is not shared. The app lists who, so you can reassign or cancel it.

If a work pattern is broken the form shows a warning: "You can still save — this is a heads-up, not a block."

## Common problems
- **I cannot see Share week with staff.** Choose a single branch in **Branch**. It does not show when "All branches" is chosen.
- **The shift is on someone who is on leave.** The board says "shift(s) held by someone on approved leave — reassign or cancel."
- **Staff say they cannot see their shifts.** They are probably still **Not shared**. Share the week.
- **I want to repeat shifts every week.** See the repeating shifts guide.

## Related guides
- [How to change or cancel a shared shift](/help/how-to-change-or-cancel-a-shared-shift)
- [How to set up repeating shifts and Auto-schedule](/help/how-to-set-up-repeating-shifts-and-auto-schedule)
- [How to find cover and handle swap requests](/help/how-to-find-cover-and-handle-swap-requests)$hc$, array['how-to-change-or-cancel-a-shared-shift','how-to-set-up-repeating-shifts-and-auto-schedule','how-to-find-cover-and-handle-swap-requests']::text[], $hc$/schedules$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-change-or-cancel-a-shared-shift$hc$, $hc$How to change or cancel a shared shift$hc$, $hc$manager$hc$, array['location_manager','entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Edit, reassign or cancel a shift, and see why it changed.$hc$, $hc$You can change any shift. A shift that is not shared yet can be edited freely. A shared shift needs a reason, and every change is kept in the history.

## Steps
1. Open **Schedules** and tap the shift on the week board.
   ![Shift actions panel](shot:schedules-shift-actions "1. Status note | 2. Edit (with a reason) | 3. Reassign / find cover | 4. Change history | 5. Cancel shift")
2. Read the note. It says "Not shared yet" or "Shared with staff".
3. To change it, tap **Edit** (or **Edit (with a reason)** for a shared shift).
4. Change **Branch**, **Assigned to**, **Date**, **Start**, **End** or **Break (min)**.
5. For a shared shift, type the **Reason for change**.
6. Tap **Save changes**.
   ![Change shift form](shot:schedules-change-shift "1. Fields | 2. Reason for change | 3. Save changes")
7. To cancel, tap **Cancel shift** (or **Cancel shift (with a reason)**).
8. Type the **Reason** and tap **Cancel shift**.
9. To see what changed, tap **Change history**.

## What happens next
A changed shared shift shows **Changed** on the board. A cancelled shift shows **Cancelled** and stays for the record. History words include Cancelled, Reassigned, Date changed, Time changed, Branch changed, Break changed and "Can’t come in (reported)".

Admins can remove a cancelled shift for good with **Delete cancelled shift**. **Setup** has an **Open log** button that lists every deleted shift, who deleted it and why.

If a person reported **Can’t come in**, their shift shows it, and a leave request is waiting for you to decide.

## Common problems
- **The Save button will not work.** A shared shift needs a **Reason for change**.
- **I cancelled by mistake.** A cancelled shift cannot be undone. Create a new shift.
- **I do not see Delete cancelled shift.** Only Company Admins and Owners can delete.

## Related guides
