  ($hc$how-to-collect-and-track-employee-documents$hc$, $hc$How to collect and track employee documents$hc$, $hc$admin$hc$, array['location_manager','entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Use the Employee checklist to see what is missing, upload on behalf of someone and waive what is not needed.$hc$, $hc$The **Employee checklist** shows which documents each person has, and which are missing, rejected or expiring.

## Steps
1. Open **Documents**.
2. Tap the **Employee checklist** tab.
3. Choose an employee.
   ![Employee checklist](shot:docs-checklist "1. Employee checklist tab | 2. Employee picker | 3. Status badges | 4. Upload on behalf / Waive")
4. Read each status: **Missing**, **Pending review**, **Approved**, **Rejected**, **Expiring**, **Archived** or **Waived**.
5. To upload for them, tap **Upload on behalf**.
6. Choose the file and tap **Upload**.
7. If the document is not needed, tap **Waive**, type a **Reason** and confirm.
8. To ask the person to upload it, use **Ask for missing details** on their record.

## What happens next
An upload on someone's behalf says "Uploaded and submitted for line manager review." Another person must still approve it.

A waived item shows **Waived** with your reason.

Admins also see **Clean up incomplete uploads**. It removes uploads started but never finished, older than 24 hours. Saved documents are not touched.

## Common problems
- **"No document requirements set up".** Requirements are created at onboarding. None were found for this person.
- **I want the employee to upload it themselves.** Use **Ask for missing details**.

## Related guides
- [How to review and approve employee documents](/help/how-to-review-and-approve-employee-documents)
- [How to ask an employee for missing details](/help/how-to-ask-an-employee-for-missing-details)$hc$, array['how-to-review-and-approve-employee-documents','how-to-ask-an-employee-for-missing-details']::text[], $hc$/documents$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-complete-your-joining-steps$hc$, $hc$How to complete your joining steps$hc$, $hc$employee$hc$, array['staff','shift_supervisor']::text[], $hc$Fill in your details, upload documents, give your salary details, accept policies and your contract.$hc$, $hc$When you are hired you see **Onboarding** in the menu. It lists the steps to finish before and after you start. You can save and come back later.

## Steps
1. Tap **Onboarding** in the menu, or tap **Open** on the Home card "Complete your joining steps".
   ![Your joining steps](shot:onboarding-my-steps "1. Progress bar | 2. Your details | 3. Documents | 4. Salary payment | 5. Contract")
2. Step 1, **Your details**: fill in the boxes and tap **Save for later**, or tap **Send to HR** when all required boxes are done.
3. Step 2, **Documents**: choose a file for each document and tap **Upload**.
4. Step 3, **Salary payment**: choose **How you are paid**, then fill **Account holder name** and **IBAN**.
5. Step 4, **Company policies**: open each policy and accept it.
6. Step 5, **Employment contract**: tap to view it, tick the agreement box and tap **Accept contract**.
7. Look for **When you can work**. Tick the days you can work, then tap **Confirm availability**.
   ![When you can work](shot:onboarding-availability "1. Day ticks | 2. Times | 3. Confirm availability")

## What happens next
Each step shows **To do**, **Done** or **Accepted**. The progress bar shows **Your joining steps**.

Your manager reviews what you send. Documents and pay details can come back as **Changes required**. Fix them and send again. When everything is ready, your manager activates your account. After that Home shows **Your first weeks** and **Your onboarding checklist**.

Your availability helps your manager plan your shifts.

## Common problems
- **"Send to HR" is greyed out.** A required box is empty. Hover or tap it to see "Still needed".
- **The IBAN is not accepted.** It starts with AE and has 23 characters.
- **I do not see Onboarding.** It only shows while you have an open onboarding.
- **The contract says "Being prepared".** HR has not uploaded it yet.

