  ($hc$how-to-find-cover-and-handle-swap-requests$hc$, $hc$How to find cover and handle swap requests$hc$, $hc$manager$hc$, array['location_manager','entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Find someone to cover a shift, offer it to a few people, and approve or reject swaps.$hc$, $hc$When someone cannot work, the app can show who is free and allowed to cover. You can pick a person yourself or send an offer to several people.

## Steps
To find cover:
1. Tap **Find cover** on the **Today** board, or tap the shift on **Schedules** and choose **Reassign / find cover**. For an empty shift choose **Find someone for this shift**.
   ![Find cover panel](shot:cover-find-sheet "1. Pick someone / Ask a few people tabs | 2. Candidate | 3. Assign")
2. To pick yourself, stay on **Pick someone**. Only people who are free and allowed to work are listed.
3. Tap a person.
4. Type a **Note for the shift history** if asked.
5. Tap **Assign**.

To offer the shift to a few people:
1. Tap **Ask a few people**.
2. Tick the people to ask.
3. Check the **Message**. Edit it if you want.
4. Tap **Send offer to** and the number.
   ![Offer shift to a few people](shot:cover-offer-panel "1. People ticks | 2. Message | 3. Send offer")

To decide a swap:
1. On **Schedules**, find **Swap requests awaiting your decision**.
2. Read who asks and who will cover.
3. Tap **Approve** or **Reject**.
   ![Swap requests awaiting your decision](shot:cover-swap-requests "1. Swap row | 2. Reject | 3. Approve")

## What happens next
After **Assign** the app says "... now covers ...". The shift moves to that person.

An offer goes to the people you ticked. The first to accept gets the shift and you are notified. Others who were offered see it closed. Suggestions come from scheduling rules, and nothing is sent until you press Send.

Swaps: **Approve** says "Swap approved — the shift has been reassigned." **Reject** says "Swap rejected." Staff see Approved or Not approved. **Swap history** lists older swaps.

People who cannot work the shift are listed under **Not eligible** with the reason.

## Common problems
- **Nobody is eligible.** The app says so and shows reasons. Change the shift time or ask someone from another branch.
- **Staff cannot ask for cover.** Shift handovers are off. Admins can switch on "Let staff hand shifts to each other" in **Setup**.
- **The offer was not sent to someone.** The app lists who was skipped and why.

## Related guides
- [How to change or cancel a shared shift](/help/how-to-change-or-cancel-a-shared-shift)
- [How to approve or decline leave](/help/how-to-approve-or-decline-leave)
- [How to use the Today board](/help/how-to-use-the-today-board)$hc$, array['how-to-change-or-cancel-a-shared-shift','how-to-approve-or-decline-leave','how-to-use-the-today-board']::text[], $hc$/schedules$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-give-someone-access-and-send-an-invite$hc$, $hc$How to give someone access and send an invite$hc$, $hc$admin$hc$, array['entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Give a person a login with the right role, send the invite email and turn access off when they leave.$hc$, $hc$A person needs a login before they can use the app. You give access in **Admin**, then send the invite email. They tap the link and set a password.

## Steps
1. Tap **Admin** in the menu, then the **Users & access** tab.
2. Tap **Grant access**.
   ![Users and access list](shot:admin-users-tab "1. Users & access tab | 2. Grant access | 3. Send invite / Resend invite | 4. Revoke access")
3. Type their **Email**.
4. Choose a **Role**: Owner, Company Admin, Branch Manager, Shift Supervisor or Employee. The hint under the box explains each one.
5. Choose the **Company** and **Branch** if asked.
6. Choose the **Linked employee**. Only employees who have no login are listed.
7. Tap **Grant access**.
   ![Grant access form](shot:admin-grant-access "1. Email | 2. Role | 3. Linked employee | 4. Grant access")
8. In the list, tap **Send invite** next to the person.
9. If they never used the link, tap **Resend invite**.

To turn access off:
1. Tap **Revoke access** next to the person.
2. Type the **Reason**.
3. Tap **Revoke access** to confirm.

## What happens next
The app says "Invitation email sent to ...". If the person already has a login, it says access is applied and they can sign in now.

The list shows **Invite not sent yet** or **Invite not yet accepted**, and **Last sign-in**. When the person taps the link they choose a password. See the sign-in guide.

After you revoke access the person sees "Your access is inactive" when they sign in.

Role summary: Employees use their own schedule, clock, leave, documents and payslips. A Shift Supervisor is an employee who also runs the floor at their branch and cannot see pay, leave, documents or profiles, or build the schedule. A Branch Manager runs one branch. A Company Admin runs one company. The Owner has full access. Only the Owner can grant Owner access.

## Common problems
- **"Grant access to ... first, then send the invite."** You must grant access before you invite.
- **"Too many emails have been sent recently."** Wait a few minutes, then use **Resend invite**.
- **The person cannot find the email.** Ask them to check spam, then resend.
- **The linked employee is missing.** They already have a login, or have no record yet. Add them in **People**.
- **A supervisor needs a branch.** Set the employee's home branch first.

## Related guides
- [Quick start for new staff](/help/quick-start-for-new-staff)
