  ($hc$how-to-offboard-an-employee$hc$, $hc$How to offboard an employee$hc$, $hc$admin$hc$, array['entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Record notice and last working day, finish the leaving checklist and start the final settlement.$hc$, $hc$Offboarding keeps a person's leaving in one place: notice, last working day, the leaving checklist and the final settlement. Branch Managers can see the cases for their branch. Company Admins and Owners start them.

## Steps
1. Tap **Offboarding** in the menu. You can also open a person's record and tap **Start offboarding**.
2. Tap **Start offboarding**.
   ![Offboarding list](shot:offboarding-list "1. Offboarding menu | 2. Start offboarding | 3. Tabs Leaving / Left / Cancelled")
3. Choose the **Employee**.
4. Choose the **Type**, for example Resignation, Termination with notice or End of limited contract.
5. Check **Ended by**.
6. Set **Notice given on** and **Last working day**.
7. Tick **Leaving the UAE (not joining another UAE employer)** if it applies.
8. If the notice is short, answer **Why is the notice shorter?**
9. Type the **Reason**. Only HR sees it, not the branch manager.
10. Tap **Start offboarding** to confirm.
    ![Start offboarding form](shot:offboarding-start-form "1. Employee | 2. Type | 3. Notice given on / Last working day | 4. Reason | 5. Start offboarding")
11. Open the case. Work through the **Checklist**. Tap **Done** on each item, or mark one **Not needed** with a reason.
12. Under **Final settlement**, tap **Start settlement in Payroll**. Then finish the payment in **Payroll**.
13. When everything is done, tap **Finish offboarding**.
    ![Offboarding case](shot:offboarding-case "1. Checklist Done | 2. Start settlement in Payroll | 3. Finish offboarding")

## What happens next
The list has three tabs: **Leaving**, **Left** and **Cancelled**. Starting offboarding sets the last working day for payroll and creates the leaving checklist.

The final settlement should be paid within 14 days of the last working day. The page shows the due date. An off-cycle payroll run opens. When it is paid the checklist item completes by itself.

**Finish offboarding** only works after the last working day and when the required checklist is finished. Use **Change dates** if the dates move. Use **Cancel offboarding** if the person stays.

## Common problems
- **Finish offboarding is greyed.** Hover to read: "After the last working day" or "Finish the required checklist first".
- **I do not see Start offboarding.** Only Company Admins and Owners can start it.
- **Payroll cannot be opened.** You need payroll access, or ask a payroll admin.

## Related guides
- [How to run an off-cycle or final settlement payroll](/help/how-to-run-an-off-cycle-or-final-settlement-payroll)
- [How to view and manage your team](/help/how-to-view-and-manage-your-team)
- [How to run payroll for a month](/help/how-to-run-payroll)$hc$, array['how-to-run-an-off-cycle-or-final-settlement-payroll','how-to-view-and-manage-your-team','how-to-run-payroll']::text[], $hc$/offboarding$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-onboard-a-new-employee$hc$, $hc$How to onboard a new employee$hc$, $hc$admin$hc$, array['entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Start onboarding, invite the person, review what they send and activate them.$hc$, $hc$Onboarding takes a new hire from offer to their first weeks. You start it, invite the person, review what they send, and activate them.

## Steps
1. Tap **Onboarding** in the menu.
2. Tap **Start onboarding**. For an accepted offer start from **Recruiting** instead.
   ![Onboarding dashboard](shot:onboarding-dashboard "1. Start onboarding | 2. KPI cards | 3. List tabs")
3. Choose **Direct hire** or **Existing pre-boarding employee**.
4. For a direct hire fill in **Full name (as on passport)**, **Email**, **Mobile**, **Employment type**, **Branch**, **Job**, **Start date** and **Reporting manager**.
   ![Start onboarding form](shot:onboarding-start-form "1. Direct hire | 2. Name/Email | 3. Branch/Job/Start date | 4. Start onboarding")
5. Tap **Start onboarding**.
6. Open the person from **New starters**. Tap **Invite to portal**.
7. Under **Starting pay** tap **Enter pay**. Someone else with payroll approval must tap **Approve pay**.
8. Review **Waiting for your review**. Tap **Approve** or **Request changes** for each part.
9. Review **Documents**: **Approve**, **Reject**, **Mark done** or **Upload contract**.
10. Check **Salary payment details**. Tap **Verify** or **Reject**.
11. Fix anything under **Problems**. Tap **Resolve** when done.
12. Tap **Approve and activate** when it is ready.
    ![Onboarding workspace](shot:onboarding-workspace "1. Invite to portal | 2. Waiting for your review | 3. Starting pay | 4. Approve and activate")

## What happens next
The new person gets an email invitation, and signs in to complete their joining steps. The list tabs show where everyone is: **All open**, **Starting soon**, **Waiting for employee**, **To review**, **Blocked**, **Ready to activate**, **Started**, **Working, onboarding not finished**, **Completed** and **Cancelled**.

Statuses include Setting up, Waiting for employee, Under review, Changes required, Blocked, Ready to activate, Activated, Day one, First weeks and Completed.

**Approve and activate** is only on when nothing blocks it. If you must activate anyway, use **Activate anyway**. Then **Record day one** and finally **Close onboarding**.

Other buttons: **Resend invitation** or **Reissue invitation**, **Raise a problem** (tick "Blocks activation until resolved" if needed), **Cancel onboarding**. A person who never starts can be recorded with **Record withdrawal**.

Other tabs: **Probation**, **Visas & permits** (admins), **Reports** and **Setup** (admins) for the checklist templates.

## Common problems
- **Approve and activate is greyed.** The hover text says "Resolve the blocking items first".
- **The invitation expired.** Tap **Reissue invitation**.
- **I cannot approve the pay I entered.** A different person with payroll approval must do it.
- **No email address.** Add one in **Setup** first. The page says so.

