- [How to set a work pattern and availability](/help/how-to-set-work-pattern-and-availability)
- [How to offboard an employee](/help/how-to-offboard-an-employee)$hc$, array['how-to-collect-and-track-employee-documents','how-to-set-work-pattern-and-availability','how-to-offboard-an-employee']::text[], $hc$/onboarding$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-record-payroll-payments$hc$, $hc$How to record payroll payments$hc$, $hc$admin$hc$, array['entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Export a payment list for the bank, then record each payment once the money has gone.$hc$, $hc$Payments are recorded after payroll is approved. Recording a payment tells the app the person has been paid. Only record it when the money has really left.

## Steps
1. Open **Payroll** and choose the month.
2. Tick the approved people.
3. Tap **Export payment list**. This downloads a CSV of outstanding amounts for your bank.
   ![Bulk bar with payment actions](shot:payroll-pay-bulk "1. Tick people | 2. Export payment list | 3. Record payment")
4. Send the payments from your bank.
5. When the bank confirms, tick the people and tap **Record payment**.
6. In **Result**, choose **Paid (confirmed by bank)**.
7. Set **Date paid**. It cannot be in the future.
8. Choose the **Method**: Bank transfer, WPS agent / exchange, Exchange house, Cash or Cheque.
9. Add a **Reference** if you have one.
10. Tap **Preview**.
11. Tap **Record for** and the number of employees.
    ![Record payment form](shot:payroll-record-payment "1. Result | 2. Date paid | 3. Method | 4. Reference | 5. Preview | 6. Record for n employees")

## What happens next
Each person's outstanding amount is paid in full unless you type an amount in **Amount**. The **Paid** box on the page goes up, and the page says how much is still to pay.

If a payment fails, choose **Failed / returned** and type **Why it failed**. It is kept for the record but does not count as paid.

Exporting never marks anyone paid. The file is not a WPS SIF file. Anything in **Payment lists exported** shows older exports. If a record is changed, an old export that contains it is marked void.

Accountants and payroll admins can record payments. A record with a payment cannot go back to draft. Use a correction instead.

## Common problems
- **I cannot choose today's date in the future.** Record the payment on the day the bank sends it.
- **Record payment is missing.** The person is not approved yet, or you have no payment permission.
- **I marked the wrong person.** Ask the Owner or a payroll admin how to correct it. We could not confirm a "undo payment" button.

## Related guides
- [How to run payroll for a month](/help/how-to-run-payroll)
- [How to set the pay date and schedule payslips](/help/how-to-set-pay-date-and-schedule-payslips)
- [How to correct payroll after approval](/help/how-to-correct-payroll-after-approval)$hc$, array['how-to-run-payroll','how-to-set-pay-date-and-schedule-payslips','how-to-correct-payroll-after-approval']::text[], $hc$/payroll$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-request-leave$hc$, $hc$How to request leave$hc$, $hc$employee$hc$, array['staff','shift_supervisor']::text[], $hc$Ask for annual or sick leave, check your balance and cancel a request that is still waiting.$hc$, $hc$Use the **Leave** page to ask for days off. Your manager decides. You can see your balance and every request you made.

## Steps
1. Tap **Leave** in the menu. The page is called **My leave**.
2. Look at **Balances** to see how many days you have.
   ![My leave page with balances](shot:leave-my-leave "1. Leave menu | 2. Balances | 3. Request leave | 4. Your requests")
3. Tap **Request leave**.
4. Choose a **Leave type**: Annual Leave or Sick Leave.
5. Choose the **Start date**.
6. Choose the **End date**.
7. Check the line "You have ... days of ... left."
8. Add a **Reason (optional)**.
9. Tap **Submit request**.
   ![Request leave form](shot:leave-request-form "1. Leave type | 2. Start date | 3. End date | 4. Balance line | 5. Submit request")

To cancel a request:
1. Find it under **Your requests**.
2. Tap **Cancel** (only shown while it is Pending).
3. Confirm in the box.

## What happens next
The app says "Leave request submitted — your manager needs to approve it." Your request shows **Pending**.

The branch manager is told about your request. They can **Approve** or **Reject** it. Owners and Company Admins can also decide.

- **Approved**: your balance goes down and you are told with a notification.
- **Rejected**: you are told, and a manager's note may show under the request.
- **Cancelled**: you cancelled it. Any balance held for it is given back.

If you ask for more days than you have, the form warns "This is more than your balance — your manager may refuse it." Only an Owner or Company Admin can approve with an override.

You cannot cancel a request once it is Approved or Rejected. Talk to your manager.

## Common problems
- **"Leave isn’t set up for you yet."** Ask your manager to set up your leave.
- **The end date error.** The end date must be the same as or after the start date.
- **There is no Cancel button.** Only Pending requests can be cancelled.
- **I need leave for a day I am sick.** You can also use **Can’t come in** on your shift. It sends a leave request for you.

