  ($hc$how-to-review-and-approve-employee-documents$hc$, $hc$How to review and approve employee documents$hc$, $hc$manager$hc$, array['location_manager','entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Check uploaded documents, approve or reject them, upload on someone's behalf and follow the second-person rule.$hc$, $hc$When an employee uploads a document, someone else must review it. Use the **Document register** to see everything and decide.

## Steps
1. Tap **Documents** in the menu.
2. Stay on the **Document register** tab.
3. Use **Review status** and set it to **Pending review**. You can also search or filter by **Document type** and expiry.
   ![Document register](shot:docs-register "1. Document register tab | 2. Review status / Document type filters | 3. Review")
4. Tap **Review** on a row.
5. Tap **View file** to open it.
6. Tap **Approve** if it is correct.
7. Or tap **Reject**, type the **Rejection reason (required)** and confirm.
   ![Review a document](shot:docs-review-drawer "1. View file | 2. Version history | 3. Reject | 4. Approve")

Other actions on an approved document:
- **View** opens the file.
- **Renew** starts a renewal on their behalf.
- **Archive** keeps it on record but stops it showing as current.
- **Discard** removes a pending upload that was never made current. This cannot be undone.

## What happens next
The document shows **Approved** or **Rejected**. The employee sees the rejection reason and can resubmit. An approved document stays **Current**. Expiry is shown separately as **Expiring soon**, **Expired** or **No expiry set**.

The second-person rule: you cannot review your own upload. The app says "You uploaded this document, so someone else must review it." The only exception is the Owner. Owner uploads are approved at once.

Branch Managers can only review ordinary documents such as a health card. Passport, visa, Emirates ID, contracts, offer letters, bank and salary documents need a Company Admin or Owner, and are hidden from Branch Managers. A Company Admin's own upload of a sensitive document needs the Owner.

An Owner can switch on "Let Company Admins approve their own uploads". It only covers ordinary documents.

## Common problems
- **I cannot approve it.** You uploaded it, or it is a sensitive document and you are a Branch Manager.
- **Some document types are missing for me.** Branch Managers cannot see sensitive types.
- **"This employee already has a current document of that type."** Use **Renew** on the existing one.
- **Only PDF, JPG and PNG are accepted.** Ask for a different file type.

## Related guides
- [How to ask an employee for missing details](/help/how-to-ask-an-employee-for-missing-details)
- [How to collect and track employee documents](/help/how-to-collect-and-track-employee-documents)
- [How to upload or renew a document](/help/how-to-upload-or-renew-a-document)$hc$, array['how-to-ask-an-employee-for-missing-details','how-to-collect-and-track-employee-documents','how-to-upload-or-renew-a-document']::text[], $hc$/documents$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-review-attendance$hc$, $hc$How to review attendance and correct a record$hc$, $hc$manager$hc$, array['shift_supervisor','location_manager','entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Find clock problems, confirm a suggested clock-out, correct a clock-in or clock-out, and change paid hours.$hc$, $hc$**Attendance** compares planned shifts with real clock-ins. You can fix mistakes. Every correction keeps the original record and the reason.

## Steps
1. Tap **Attendance** in the menu.
2. Choose **Branch**, **From** and **To**, then tap **Refresh**.
3. Open the **Exceptions** tab. Supervisors see this view only.
   ![Attendance exceptions](shot:attendance-exceptions "1. Branch/From/To | 2. Exceptions tab | 3. Confirm / Change… / Dismiss | 4. Correct")
4. Find the problem. Types are: **Missing clock-out**, **Didn’t clock in**, **Clock-in without a shift**, **Late clock-in**.
5. If you see **Suggested clock-out**, tap **Confirm** to accept the time. Tap **Dismiss** to ignore it. Tap **Change…** to set another time.
6. Otherwise tap **Correct**.
7. Set **New clock-in (Dubai time)** and **New clock-out (Dubai time)**. Leave a box empty to keep it.
8. Type the **Reason**. The employee can see it.
9. Tap **Review changes**, then **Save correction**.
   ![Correct attendance form](shot:attendance-correct-form "1. New clock-in | 2. New clock-out | 3. Reason | 4. Review changes")

To change paid hours (managers and admins):
1. Open the **Overview** tab.
2. Tap **Change paid hours** on a row.
3. Set the new **Hours** and **Minutes**, and a **Reason**.
4. Tap **Send for approval**.
5. Open **Hours changes** to see the request. Approvers tap **Apply** or **Reject**.

## What happens next
After a correction the app says the original record is kept in the audit trail. The employee sees **Corrected** and your reason in their last 30 days.

Hours changes show **Pending**, then applied or rejected. Rejecting needs a **Reason for rejecting**. If a shift is already in payroll, **Change paid hours** is off ("Already in payroll").

The tiles show **Shifts in range**, **Exceptions**, **Hours changes waiting** and **Hours to pay**. If there are no payable shifts, tap **Load hours from shifts**.

## Common problems
- **"You cannot correct your own record."** Ask another manager.
- **"Times cannot be in the future."** Pick a time in the past.
- **"No clock-in to correct".** The person never clocked in. Ask them to clock in, or tell payroll.
- **I do not see Overview or Hours changes.** Shift supervisors only see exceptions and corrections, never pay time.

## Related guides
- [How to use the Today board](/help/how-to-use-the-today-board)
- [How to clock in and out](/help/how-to-clock-in-and-out)
- [How to prepare and approve payroll](/help/how-to-run-payroll)$hc$, array['how-to-use-the-today-board','how-to-clock-in-and-out','how-to-run-payroll']::text[], $hc$/attendance$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-run-an-off-cycle-or-final-settlement-payroll$hc$, $hc$How to run an off-cycle or final settlement payroll$hc$, $hc$admin$hc$, array['entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Pay someone outside the monthly run, for example a final settlement.$hc$, $hc$An off-cycle payroll is a separate run for a one-off payment or a final settlement. It is not part of the monthly run.

## Steps
1. Open **Payroll**.
2. Tap **Off-cycle / final settlement**.
   ![Off-cycle button](shot:payroll-offcycle-button "1. Off-cycle / final settlement")
3. Type a **Label**, for example "Final settlement – name".
4. Set the **Pay date**.
5. Add a **Salary month (optional)** if the payslip should show a month.
6. Tap **Create**.
   ![Off-cycle form](shot:payroll-offcycle-form "1. Label | 2. Pay date | 3. Salary month | 4. Create")
7. Under **Add an employee to this off-cycle payroll**, choose the person and tap **Add**.
8. Open their record. Fill **Leaving (final settlement)** with the **Last working day** and the settlement items.
9. Approve, record payment and publish as normal.

## What happens next
The run appears in the month list with its label. People are prepared in it like in a monthly run. Items such as **End-of-service gratuity**, **Leave encashment** and **Notice pay** are available as one-off earnings.

For normal monthly salary, use **Prepare payroll** for that month instead.

## Common problems
- **Create is greyed.** Type a **Label** first.
- **The person is not in the list.** Only people not already in this run can be added.
- **I need to start offboarding first.** See the offboarding guide.

## Related guides
- [How to run payroll for a month](/help/how-to-run-payroll)
- [How to offboard an employee](/help/how-to-offboard-an-employee)
- [How to record payroll payments](/help/how-to-record-payroll-payments)$hc$, array['how-to-run-payroll','how-to-offboard-an-employee','how-to-record-payroll-payments']::text[], $hc$/payroll$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-run-payroll$hc$, $hc$How to run payroll for a month$hc$, $hc$admin$hc$, array['entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Pick the month, prepare salaries, check each person, approve, then record payments and publish payslips.$hc$, $hc$The **Payroll** page runs the whole month in one place. The order is: month, employees, salary preparation, check and approve, pay date, payments, payslips. Every amount opens to show how it was calculated.

## Steps
1. Tap **Payroll** in the menu.
2. Choose the month in **Payroll month**. For a new month, pick it in **Start another month** and tap **Prepare payroll**.
   ![Payroll month and prepare](shot:payroll-month-prepare "1. Payroll menu | 2. Payroll month | 3. Start another month | 4. Prepare payroll | 5. Readiness checklist")
3. Read the checklist at the top. Fix anything marked **Must fix**. Items marked **Worth a look** are only warnings.
4. Look at **What changed since** last month. Tap **Explain in plain words** if you want.
5. Check the table: **Fixed pay**, **Extra earnings**, **Deductions**, **Net pay** and **Status**. Rows marked **Fix needed** or **Check** need attention.
6. Tap a person to open the record. Check **Hours this month**, **Earnings**, **Deductions** and **Pay and allowances**.
   ![Payroll record for one employee](shot:payroll-record-drawer "1. Net pay | 2. Hours this month | 3. Earnings / Deductions | 4. Recalculate | 5. Approve")
7. If hours or pay setup changed, tap **Recalculate**.
8. In **Pay date and payslips**, tap **Change dates** to set the pay date and when payslips are published.
9. Tick **Select all** in the table, or tick some people.
10. Tap **Approve**. In review mode tap **Send for review** first.
    ![Payroll bulk actions](shot:payroll-bulk-bar "1. Select all | 2. Status column | 3. Bulk bar main button")
11. Then record payments and publish payslips.

## What happens next
Each person shows one status: **Not prepared**, **Draft**, **In review**, **Approved**, then **Published** once the payslip is shared. A person can show **Fix needed** or **Check**.

The top boxes show **Employees**, **Total net payroll**, **Paid** (and how much is "still to pay") and **Needs a look**. When everyone is paid and published the page says "This month is finished".

How approval works depends on **Settings**: **Two people: one prepares, another approves**, **Prepare → review → approve**, or Owner single step. In the standard setting a second person must approve.

Prepare uses salary, allowances, leave, overtime, tips and advances. Branch managers enter hours and tips only. They never see pay amounts.

Other buttons at the top: **Distribute tips**, **Advances**, **Reports** and **Settings**.

## Common problems
- **"Fix needed" on someone.** Open them and read the red items. Common ones are missing pay or bank details.
- **Approve is missing or greyed.** You may not have approval permission, or the person is not sent for review. The record says why.
- **I am the one who prepared it.** In the standard setting a second person must approve.
- **A message says payroll uses the standard settings.** Tap **Review settings** and check them once before your first payroll.
- **Someone is "Not prepared".** Tap **Prepare** on their row.

