- [How to add tips, advances and extra pay](/help/how-to-add-tips-advances-and-extra-pay)$hc$, array['how-to-record-payroll-payments','how-to-set-pay-date-and-schedule-payslips','how-to-correct-payroll-after-approval','how-to-add-tips-advances-and-extra-pay']::text[], $hc$/payroll$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-set-opening-hours-and-staffing-needs$hc$, $hc$How to set opening hours and staffing needs$hc$, $hc$admin$hc$, array['entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Tell the scheduler when each branch is open and how many people it needs.$hc$, $hc$Auto-schedule only plans for branches that have opening hours. Staffing needs say how many people you need and when.

## Steps
1. Open **Schedules**, then the **Setup** tab.
2. Find **Opening hours and staffing needs**.
3. Tap **Branch setup**.
   ![Setup tab](shot:schedules-setup-tab "1. Setup tab | 2. Branch setup | 3. Staff self-service tick box")
4. Choose the branch at the top.
5. Under **Opening hours**, set the open and close time for each day. Untick a day to mark it **Closed**.
6. Tap "Use ... for all open days" to copy times.
7. Under **Staffing needs**, tap **+ Add staffing need**.
8. Set **People needed**, the role, the day, and the **from** and **to** times.
   ![Branch setup panel](shot:branch-setup-sheet "1. Branch tabs | 2. Opening hours | 3. + Add staffing need | 4. Save")
9. Tap **Save** with the branch name.

## What happens next
The app says "Saved opening hours and staffing needs for ...". Saving replaces all needs for that branch.

With no staffing needs, the scheduler plans 1 person for the whole opening time. A branch with no opening hours shows "Not set up yet — nothing will be auto-scheduled here". Times that end after midnight show **next day**.

In **Setup**, admins also find **Staff self-service**, where a tick box lets staff hand shifts to each other. A manager still approves each handover. Owners also see a tick box for cross-branch claims.

## Common problems
- **"No opening hours yet" in Auto-schedule.** Set them here first.
- **Unsaved changes.** The panel shows "Unsaved changes". Tap **Save** before closing.
- **Staff cannot ask for cover.** Tick the shift handover box in **Staff self-service**.

## Related guides
- [How to set up repeating shifts and Auto-schedule](/help/how-to-set-up-repeating-shifts-and-auto-schedule)
- [How to set a work pattern and availability](/help/how-to-set-work-pattern-and-availability)$hc$, array['how-to-set-up-repeating-shifts-and-auto-schedule','how-to-set-work-pattern-and-availability']::text[], $hc$/schedules$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-set-pay-date-and-schedule-payslips$hc$, $hc$How to set the pay date and schedule payslips$hc$, $hc$admin$hc$, array['entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Choose the pay date, publish payslips by hand or on a schedule, and see what staff will see.$hc$, $hc$Each month has a pay date and a payslip publishing plan. Staff only see a payslip after it is published.

## Steps
1. Open **Payroll** and choose the month.
2. Find **Pay date and payslips**. It shows **Pay date** and **Payslips**.
   ![Pay date and payslips panel](shot:payroll-pay-date-panel "1. Pay date | 2. Payslips plan | 3. Change dates")
3. Tap **Change dates**.
4. Set **Pay date (when the salary goes to the bank)**. It can be in the future. Leave it empty to use the payroll settings.
5. Set **Publish payslips on (Dubai time)**. Leave it empty to publish by hand.
6. Tick **Only publish payslips for people whose payment is recorded** if you want.
7. Tap **Save dates**.
8. To publish by hand: tick the approved people, tap **Publish payslips** and confirm.
9. To stop a schedule, tap **Stop automatic publishing**.
   ![Change dates form](shot:payroll-change-dates "1. Pay date | 2. Publish payslips on | 3. Only publish ... tick | 4. Save dates")

## What happens next
The page says "Payslips will be published on ..." for everyone approved (and paid, if you ticked that box). Employees are notified and can view and download their payslip under **Payslips**.

If no pay date is set, the page shows "(from payroll settings)". The usual pay day is set in **Settings** as "Pay day (of the following month)".

A published payslip cannot be edited. Use a correction. Payslip lists also appear in **Download payslips** in the bulk bar.

## Common problems
- **Payslips did not publish on time.** Check people were Approved, and Paid if you ticked the box.
- **Staff say they have no payslip.** It is not published yet.
- **Settings has a "Note printed on payslips" box.** Use it for a message on every payslip.

## Related guides
- [How to run payroll for a month](/help/how-to-run-payroll)
- [How to record payroll payments](/help/how-to-record-payroll-payments)
- [How to view and download payslips](/help/how-to-view-and-download-payslips)$hc$, array['how-to-run-payroll','how-to-record-payroll-payments','how-to-view-and-download-payslips']::text[], $hc$/payroll$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-set-up-repeating-shifts-and-auto-schedule$hc$, $hc$How to set up repeating shifts and Auto-schedule$hc$, $hc$manager$hc$, array['location_manager','entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Create weekly repeating shifts, and let Auto-schedule plan a period from opening hours and staffing needs.$hc$, $hc$Repeating shifts save time for fixed rotas. Auto-schedule (admins only) builds a draft roster for you. Both create shifts that are not shared until you share them.

## Steps
To use repeating shifts (Branch Managers and admins):
1. Open **Schedules**, then the **Repeating shifts** tab. Admins see it as **Setup**.
2. Tap **New repeating shift**.
3. Choose **Branch**, **Employee**, **Day of week**, **Start**, **End** and **Break (min)**.
4. Set **Effective from**. Add **Effective to (optional)** if it ends.
   ![New repeating shift form](shot:schedules-repeating-form "1. Branch/Employee | 2. Day of week | 3. Start/End | 4. Effective from")
5. Save it.
6. In **Weekly repeating shifts**, choose a **Branch**, **Period start** and **Period end**.
7. Tap **Create shifts**.
8. Check them on the **Week** tab.
9. Tap **Share with staff** and confirm.

To use Auto-schedule (Company Admin and Owner):
1. Open **Schedules**, then the **Auto-schedule** tab.
2. Step 1: choose **Next week**, **Next 7 days**, **Next 2 weeks** or **Custom**.
3. Step 2: tick the branches. Tap **Set up** if a branch has no opening hours.
4. Step 3: tap **Preview plan**.
   ![Auto-schedule preview](shot:auto-schedule-preview "1. Period | 2. Branches | 3. Preview plan | 4. Create button")
5. Read the plan.
6. Tap **Create** to save the shifts as "(not shared yet)".
7. Go to the **Week** tab and share the week.

## What happens next
Auto-schedule plans from opening hours, staffing needs, availability, approved leave and weekly limits (48 hours, 6 days). People from the home branch go first. Nothing is saved until you create the shifts. If you change the period or branches, tap **Update preview** first.

Shifts that would overlap existing shifts are skipped. The app says how many were created.

## Common problems
- **"No opening hours yet".** Set opening hours first. See the opening hours guide.
- **"No new shifts".** Everyone already has these shifts, or they would overlap.
- **I do not see Auto-schedule.** It is only for Company Admins and Owners.

## Related guides
- [How to build and share a weekly schedule](/help/how-to-build-and-share-a-weekly-schedule)
- [How to set opening hours and staffing needs](/help/how-to-set-opening-hours-and-staffing-needs)
- [How to set a work pattern and availability](/help/how-to-set-work-pattern-and-availability)$hc$, array['how-to-build-and-share-a-weekly-schedule','how-to-set-opening-hours-and-staffing-needs','how-to-set-work-pattern-and-availability']::text[], $hc$/schedules$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-set-work-pattern-and-availability$hc$, $hc$How to set a work pattern and availability$hc$, $hc$admin$hc$, array['location_manager','entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Set how many days a person works, which days off they have, and see the availability they gave.$hc$, $hc$A work pattern tells the schedule how many days a person works and when they have days off. Shift forms and Auto-schedule use it to warn you or plan correctly.

## Steps
1. Open **People** and tap the person.
2. Open the **Schedule** tab.
3. Find the **Work pattern** card.
   ![Work pattern card](shot:work-pattern-card "1. Schedule tab | 2. Work pattern | 3. Set pattern / Edit | 4. Availability")
4. Tap **Set pattern** (or **Edit**). Company Admins and Owners can edit it.
5. Choose **Working days per week**.
6. Under **Days off**, choose **Flexible** (the scheduler decides) or **Fixed days** (always the same days). For fixed days, tap the days.
7. Choose **Shift type**: **Any shift** or **Morning only** (shifts that start before 10:00).
8. Tap **Save pattern**.
   ![Work pattern editor](shot:work-pattern-editor "1. Working days per week | 2. Days off | 3. Shift type | 4. Save pattern")

## What happens next
The card says "Saved. The auto-scheduler and shift forms now use this pattern."

With no pattern, the scheduler allows up to 6 days a week, on any day. A broken pattern does not block you: the shift form shows "You can still save — this is a heads-up, not a block."

Below the pattern, **Availability** shows each day: **Day off**, **Unavailable**, a time range, **Any time** or **Not set**. Staff give this themselves in their onboarding step "When you can work". If none is on file, the person counts as available any day and any time.

To remove a pattern, use the remove option on the card and confirm.

## Common problems
- **I cannot see Set pattern.** Only Company Admins and Owners can edit it.
- **I cannot change someone's availability.** The page only shows it. We could not find a screen where staff change it after onboarding.
- **Auto-schedule ignores a day.** Check that person's days off and availability.

## Related guides
- [How to set up repeating shifts and Auto-schedule](/help/how-to-set-up-repeating-shifts-and-auto-schedule)
