- [Update your profile and contact details](/help/update-your-profile-and-contact-details)$hc$, array['quick-start-for-new-staff','update-your-profile-and-contact-details']::text[], $hc$/sign-in$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-upload-or-renew-a-document$hc$, $hc$How to upload or renew a document$hc$, $hc$employee$hc$, array['staff','shift_supervisor']::text[], $hc$Upload a document your manager asked for, send a new copy of an expiring document, and fix a rejected one.$hc$, $hc$Your manager may ask for a document such as a passport copy or visa. You may also need to send a new copy when a document is about to expire. You do both in **Documents**.

## Steps
To upload a document your manager asked for:
1. Open **Home**.
2. Under **Your manager needs something**, tap **Upload document**.
   ![Home card asking for a document](shot:docs-home-request "1. Request card | 2. Upload document")
3. The upload form opens. Check the **Document type**.
4. Choose the **File**. Only PDF, JPG and PNG files work.
5. Add an **Expiry date (optional)** if the document has one.
6. Add **Notes (optional)** if you need to.
7. Tap **Upload**.
   ![Upload document form](shot:docs-upload-form "1. Document type | 2. Expiry date | 3. File | 4. Upload")

You can also open **Documents** in the menu. Under **Your manager needs these**, tap **Upload**.

To renew an expiring document:
1. Open **Documents**. The page is called **My documents**.
2. Find the document under **Your documents**.
3. Tap **Upload new copy**.
   ![My documents with Upload new copy](shot:docs-my-documents "1. Documents menu | 2. Expiring badge | 3. Upload new copy")
4. Add the **New expiry date (optional)**.
5. Choose the **File**, then submit.

To fix a rejected document:
1. Find it under **Your manager needs these**. It says **Rejected** and shows the reason.
2. Tap **Resubmit**.

## What happens next
After you upload, the app says "Uploaded — pending review." Your document shows **Pending review**. Someone else must check it. You cannot approve your own upload. A manager or admin then approves or rejects it.

- **Approved**: your document is saved as current.
- **Rejected**: the reason is shown. Send a new file with **Resubmit**.
- **Expiring** or **Expired**: you can upload a new copy. You can only upload a new copy when it is expiring or expired.

When you renew, your old approved copy stays current until the new one is approved. You see "Your renewal is pending review."

Tap **View** to open a file.

## Common problems
- **"Only PDF, JPG and PNG files are accepted."** Convert or take a photo and save it as JPG or PNG.
- **I do not see Upload new copy.** The document is not close to expiry yet. It shows 60 days before it expires.
- **My renewal was rejected.** Read the reason, then use **Resubmit**.
- **"The upload did not complete — please try again."** Check your internet and try again.
- **Some document types are not visible to me.** Passport, visa, contract and similar documents are only handled by Company Admins and Owners.

## Related guides
- [Update your profile and contact details](/help/update-your-profile-and-contact-details)
- [How to use notifications](/help/how-to-use-notifications)$hc$, array['update-your-profile-and-contact-details','how-to-use-notifications']::text[], $hc$/documents$hc$, date '2026-10-01'),
  ($hc$how-to-use-notifications$hc$, $hc$How to use notifications$hc$, $hc$employee$hc$, array['staff','shift_supervisor','location_manager','entity_admin','owner']::text[], $hc$Read your alerts, open the related page and mark everything as read.$hc$, $hc$Notifications tell you when something needs you or has been decided, for example a leave decision. The bell at the top shows how many are unread.

## Steps
1. Tap the bell at the top of the screen.
   ![Notification bell with unread count](shot:notifications-bell "1. Bell | 2. A notification | 3. Mark all read")
2. Tap a notification to open it. The app takes you to the related page, such as **Leave** or **Schedule**.
3. Tap **Mark all read** to clear the list.
4. For the full list, open **Notifications** in the menu.
   ![Notifications page](shot:notifications-page "1. Show unread only | 2. Mark all as read")
5. Tick **Show unread only** to hide the ones you have read.
6. Tap **Mark all as read** to clear them all.
7. Tap **Load older** to see older ones.

## What happens next
A notification is marked read when you open it. Important ones show **High priority**. When the list is empty you see "You're all caught up".

## Common problems
- **I opened a notification but nothing happened.** Some notifications have no page to open. The message itself is the information.
- **I cannot find an old notification.** Tap **Load older** at the bottom.

